WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:00.740
[Music]

00:00:02.295 --> 00:00:05.326
Well I think any cook loves to hear "that's&nbsp;delicious"

00:00:05.326 --> 00:00:09.357
but it means a lot more when the food is actually horrific.

00:00:09.505 --> 00:00:13.720
It's a dead body. It's a lung. Maybe a roadkill rat...

00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:16.041
[Music]

00:00:21.722 --> 00:00:22.760
I'm Janice Poon 

00:00:23.097 --> 00:00:27.345
and I'm the food stylist you come&nbsp;to if you want a grizzly little something for your table.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:29.366
What have I done?...

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:30.800
Roasted legs;

00:00:31.007 --> 00:00:34.016
peking style whole bodies;

00:00:34.016 --> 00:00:35.696
edible insects;

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:38.482
tiny organs for dead rats;

00:00:38.482 --> 00:00:39.880
edible snails,

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.556
ooh space whales...

00:00:41.556 --> 00:00:42.854
(raw of course).

00:00:42.854 --> 00:00:45.739
Janice can cook up a mean severed head

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:47.315
but she's pretty much a jack-of-all-trades.

00:00:47.644 --> 00:00:49.541
Just how many jobs have you had Janice?

00:00:49.837 --> 00:00:51.877
First I was an art director in an agency...

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:53.457
then a caterer;

00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:54.787
a cookbook author;

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.669
a graphic novelist;

00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:57.966
a sculptor;

00:00:58.041 --> 00:00:59.465
then a miniaturist;

00:00:59.554 --> 00:01:00.414
couturier,

00:01:00.414 --> 00:01:03.465
and uh writing... did&nbsp;I forget anything?

00:01:03.695 --> 00:01:05.908
Now back to the juicy stuff.

00:01:06.222 --> 00:01:08.427
Oh I love the reading part of the creative process.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.223
Lay back on the sofa.

00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:12.600
I read as much as possible.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:18.525
I just do a quick sketch to communicate to&nbsp;everybody the look I'm going for and narrow the field.

00:01:18.585 --> 00:01:20.835
The kitchen is really where the sorrow&nbsp;begins.

00:01:20.895 --> 00:01:24.867
That's where everything that you thought was going to work out great...

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:26.255
 doesn't...

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:31.205
and that is&nbsp;where you really start to think- well now what am I going to do?

00:01:31.644 --> 00:01:35.120
You know it's kind of yummy...

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.908
Nothing like&nbsp;a little raw hamburger to get you going.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.117
Hang on - did she just eat raw meat?

00:01:42.362 --> 00:01:48.000
As a food stylist I get all&nbsp;kinds of requests from actors who have dietary restrictions.

00:01:48.376 --> 00:01:54.091
I didn't expect, however, to get one&nbsp;
from a vampire queen who wouldn't eat meat.

00:01:54.504 --> 00:01:57.594
What I used was essentially sweet potato. 

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:58.880
That doesn't&nbsp;look like meat.

00:01:58.998 --> 00:02:02.440
Hmm... maybe I need something to make it more gummy.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.109
I'll put a bunch of glutinous flour in.

00:02:04.226 --> 00:02:08.327
Well that's a bit yellow for meat isn't it? So I'll put in some beets.

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:15.404
After a couple minutes&nbsp;of the microwave spinning around, what it needs is a little tiny flax of fat.

00:02:15.598 --> 00:02:23.519
I use chopped up rice and just plough that stuff in, oil, and that's really going to make it look visceral.

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:26.441
Surely that's&nbsp;not edible?

00:02:26.441 --> 00:02:29.426
It's not just edible... It's delicious.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.110
Any more tips and tricks?

00:02:34.861 --> 00:02:40.772
Well, one little food&nbsp;item that we have in a lot of horror movies is corn syrup.

00:02:40.772 --> 00:02:43.994
Corn syrup with food&nbsp;colouring in it to make it look like blood. 

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:53.040
Buckets and buckets and buckets of this stuff&nbsp;get used for TV shows and you just, like, pour it&nbsp;on and lick it off.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.693
I would say the duct tape of&nbsp;food styling is oil

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:06.811
because a little slick of&nbsp;oil is going to make anything look as if it just&nbsp;freshly cooked or it's just juicy and delicious.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:14.823
With fake mold if you want it to be edible you&nbsp;have to use Dutch processed cocoa, which is a black powder,

00:03:14.823 --> 00:03:18.196
spirulina powder, icing sugar, and white food colouring.

00:03:18.196 --> 00:03:24.493
You can dust them on your food and it'll look just like mold.  Furry but yummy.

00:03:25.824 --> 00:03:34.100
Sometimes I&nbsp;use toothpaste because it comes in a tube and you just throw it in your bag and that's little&nbsp;blobs of mold

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:38.199
but people don't like to eat a lot&nbsp;of toothpaste so there you go.

00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:43.980
Some of Janice's most&nbsp;gruesome dishes feature in the TV show Hannibal.

00:03:44.222 --> 00:03:49.911
When I looked at the first Hannibal script I&nbsp;thought - wow these people are crazy.

00:03:50.151 --> 00:03:51.606
Mads was the&nbsp;most adventurous.

00:03:51.756 --> 00:04:00.682
He was kind of annoyed with&nbsp;me the first day when I didn't serve up real&nbsp;lung, real brain and real liver...

00:04:00.756 --> 00:04:05.302
But then I knew&nbsp;he was going to be an adventurous eater so it&nbsp;all cut loose from there.

00:04:05.391 --> 00:04:10.640
Our final scene was to be Bedelia's dining on her own leg.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.399
The leg was the old go-to pork. 

00:04:13.399 --> 00:04:19.310
It had a marrow bone at the&nbsp;thigh end and a lamb shank at the ankle end.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:25.340
I felt I had to apologize to Gillian and I said "Gillian&nbsp;I'm sorry I made the leg so big.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.471
If I had made it the size of your leg it wouldn't have looked&nbsp;as impressive."

00:04:29.471 --> 00:04:36.032
She did say, "oh that's beautiful", which is what you really want. She didn't say&nbsp;"oh my leg looks good."

00:04:36.032 --> 00:04:37.264
[Laughter]

00:04:37.474 --> 00:04:40.321
Any final words of wisdom, Janice?

00:04:40.426 --> 00:04:44.013
Part of storytelling, of course, is that tension.

00:04:44.013 --> 00:04:49.120
Especially with horror where so many of the characters are, psychically, on a&nbsp;knife's edge.

00:04:49.299 --> 00:04:51.693
You want your food to be on a knife's edge too.

00:04:51.992 --> 00:04:53.065
You want it to teeter.

00:04:53.153 --> 00:04:53.653
Is it horrible?

00:04:53.813 --> 00:04:54.313
Is it&nbsp;delicious?

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:57.721
No. It's horrible and delicious.

